									Locked {x.state}
								</span>
							)}
						</span>
					</div>
				))
			}
		</div>
		<p class="note">Values shown are the defaults. The first three are pinned out of the box; the others pin their setting once the host sets them. Stored values a lock overrides are kept, have no effect, and are listed in one startup warning. Every MCP setting change is recorded in the settings history with who changed it.</p>
	</Section>

	<Section num="07" label="Audit and security events" title="Every layer leaves a record." lede="Beacon keeps two audit tables and writes security-relevant actions as structured log events with identifiers only. The log events are not stored by Beacon: ship them to your log pipeline and alert on them.">
